Commands:
cd - change dirctory
syntax: cd folder_name
eg: cd javalearning
====================================================
cd .. (double dot):
      It goes to the previous previos folder
Eg:  C:\Users\YourUsername\Documents>cd ..
     C:\Users\YourUsername
=====================================================
cd ..\.. (double dot backward slash double dot):
      It goes to the two previous folders
Eg:   C:\Users\YourUsername\Documents>cd ..\..
      C:\Users>
======================================================
tab key:
      Pressing tab key gives the available 
folders or files in a folder
=====================================================================     
dir command:
     This command shows all the files and folders in a folder
Eg:
      dir C:\Windows

    To display the hidden files in a folder
Eg:   dir /a

    To display the file according to their size.
Eg:   dir /o:s

    To display the files according to their alphabetical order.
Eg:   dir /o:n

    To display what a specific type of files(particular extension)
Eg:   dir *.txt -> shows all the text files
      dir *.png -> shows all the png files
===========================================================================
In cmd,Typing the file name dirctly on its folder opens it.

up and down arrow for previous and back files

cls - to clear the cmd.

=============================================================================
To create a folder using cmd:

mkdir-makedirectory

To create folder:
Eg:
  G:\My Drive>mkdir temp
  The above command creates a folder in the My Drive 

To delete folder:
Eg:
   G:\My Drive>rmdir temp
   The above command deletes the folder permanently without moving it in to the recycle bin.

To delete the folder completely including its sub folder:
    G:\My Drive>rmdir /s temp
    G:\My Drive>rmdir /s temp
    temp, Are you sure (Y/N)? Y
    The above command completely deletes the folders including its sub folders permanently without
sending it into the recycle bin.
 ======================================================================================================   

